  "review": [
    "History: Larson 1921 multi-channel instrument; earlier Marston systolic work and later Keeler refinements, no sole inventor of proven lie detection",
    "Physiological recording versus inference; CQT versus CIT, recognition not proof of guilt",
    "NRC 2003 above-chance specific-incident results in studied populations untrained in countermeasures, below perfection; screening extrapolation and bias caveats",
    "2019 Iacono-Ben-Shakhar critical review identified persistent research-quality limitations, no universal accuracy figure",
    "Sensitivity, specificity, false positives, false negatives, reliability, validity and inconclusive results distinguished; no fabricated empirical rates",
    "Senate 1994 Ames investigation: passed in 1986 and 1991, deficiencies and misplaced reassurance; no claim that Ames was trained in a successful cheating method",
    "Gary Gauger: reported inconclusive result misrepresented as failure; not a verified machine false positive; 1996 reversal and 2002 innocence pardon",
    "Honts 1994: 120 participants, 100 mock-guilty, 80 trained; roughly half defeated test per training type, not universal field success; no procedural countermeasure instructions",
    "Bond-DePaulo 2006: 206 documents, 24483 judges, roughly 54% human judgments without aids/training; not polygraph performance",
    "NIJ 2007 study/2008 summary: two specific voice-stress systems, recent drug-use reports/urine tests; about 15% of lies detected, not a general rate for all voice algorithms",
    "Cook 2012 ocular-motor task: mock crime, reading and pupil measures; no gaze-direction lie code",
    "PLOS ONE 2023 ML review: limited reused datasets, risk of bias; generalisation demands independent validation",
    "Langleben 2016 N28 concealed-number task; published advantage does not establish spontaneous-deception detector or courtroom guilt",
    "Scheffer 1998 military evidence rule upheld, not worldwide investigative ban; US EPPA most private employers with exemptions, local rules vary",
    "Approved image preserved; AI imagined interrogation, fictional readings and no real case/individual identification"
  ],
